		"posts": [
			{
				"id": "building-zero-to-one",
				"slug": "building-zero-to-one",
				"status": "published",
				"data": {
					"title": "What I've Learned Building 0-to-1 Products",
					"excerpt": "After building multiple products from scratch across fintech, govtech, and crypto, here are the patterns that consistently lead to success.",
					"content": [
						{
							"_type": "block",
							"style": "normal",
							"children": [
								{
									"_type": "span",
									"text": "Every 0-to-1 product I've built has taught me something new, but the core patterns remain remarkably consistent. Whether it was building a government-compliant CMS that now powers 9,000+ pages or launching the first crypto tax-audit platform for federal agencies, the fundamentals haven't changed."
								}
							]
						},
						{
							"_type": "block",
							"style": "h2",
							"children": [{ "_type": "span", "text": "Start with the problem, not the solution" }]
						},
						{
							"_type": "block",
							"style": "normal",
							"children": [
								{
									"_type": "span",
									"text": "The most successful products I've shipped started with deep empathy for the user's pain. At TaxBit, I spent weeks shadowing IRS auditors before writing a single user story. That investment paid off\u2014we cut their case processing time by 92% because we understood exactly where the friction was."
								}
							]
						},
						{
							"_type": "block",
							"style": "h2",
							"children": [{ "_type": "span", "text": "Ship fast, learn faster" }]
						},
						{
							"_type": "block",
							"style": "normal",
							"children": [
								{
									"_type": "span",
									"text": "Perfectionism is the enemy of 0-to-1. At Excella, we launched an MVP of the OIG hotline modernization in 8 weeks. It wasn't pretty, but it immediately reduced case triage time by 50%. That early validation gave us the political capital to invest in a full rebuild."
								}
							]
						},
						{
							"_type": "block",
							"style": "h2",
							"children": [{ "_type": "span", "text": "Revenue is the ultimate validation" }]
						},
						{
							"_type": "block",
							"style": "normal",
							"children": [
								{
									"_type": "span",
									"text": "Building the public sector business at TaxBit from $150K to $5M+ in 24 months taught me that revenue growth is the clearest signal that you're solving a real problem. Vanity metrics are comforting but revenue keeps the lights on and earns you the right to keep building."
								}
							]
						}
					]
				},
				"taxonomies": {
					"tag": ["product-management", "leadership"]
				}
			},
			{
				"id": "vibe-coding-with-claude",
				"slug": "vibe-coding-with-claude",
				"status": "published",
				"data": {
					"title": "Vibe Coding: Building a Product with Claude Code",
					"excerpt": "How I went from product manager to solo founder by building an entire app with AI-assisted development.",
					"content": [
						{
							"_type": "block",
							"style": "normal",
							"children": [
								{
									"_type": "span",
									"text": "After 15 years in product management, I decided to build something of my own. The twist? I used Claude Code to go from zero to a production nutrition-tracking app, writing nearly all the code through AI-assisted development."
								}
							]
						},
						{
							"_type": "block",
							"style": "h2",
							"children": [{ "_type": "span", "text": "Why vibe coding works for PMs" }]
						},
						{
							"_type": "block",
							"style": "normal",
							"children": [
								{
									"_type": "span",
									"text": "Product managers already think in systems, user flows, and acceptance criteria. It turns out those skills translate perfectly to prompting an LLM to write code. Instead of writing specs for engineers, I'm writing specs for Claude\u2014and the feedback loop is measured in seconds, not sprint cycles."
								}
							]
						},
						{
							"_type": "block",
							"style": "h2",
							"children": [{ "_type": "span", "text": "The hypothesis" }]
						},
						{
							"_type": "block",
							"style": "normal",
							"children": [
								{
									"_type": "span",
									"text": "Vibe Dieting started with a simple hypothesis: frontier LLMs can make macro tracking as easy as snapping a photo of your food. No more searching databases, weighing portions, or logging individual ingredients. Just take a picture, confirm the AI's analysis, and move on with your day."
								}
							]
						}
					]
				},
				"taxonomies": {
					"tag": ["technology", "product-management"]
				}
			}
		],
